  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Following National Teacher Day 2026, the Indonesian government has outlined several initiatives aimed at improving teacher welfare and professional development. President Prabowo Subianto signaled commitments to future salary increases and the expansion of training opportunities, including programs for thousands of educators to study in nine different countries starting in 2027. Additionally, the administration is focusing on digital infrastructure through the creation of remote learning studios. Legislative discussions between the House of Representatives and the Ministry of Primary and Secondary Education are actively addressing the status of honorer and PPPK teaching staff, alongside potential regulatory adjustments for prospective educators over the age of 35. These developments follow public appearances by government officials, including Cabinet Secretary Teddy Indra Wijaya, who participated in ceremonies honoring the teaching profession across the country.",
